                  <provenance type="#c"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_2">Peterborough,
                     Northamptonshire. Benedictine abbey of St Peter, St Paul, and St
                     Andrew</orgName><p>Notes of obits of Robert Wermyngton, John Rychemund, Robert
                     Keteryng, monks 'monasterii apostolorum Petri et' (sic), and names of other
                     persons scribbled at the end (cf. MS 9). Warmington and Kettering were
                     Peterborough estates.</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="#rejected"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_62">Bourne,
                     Lincolnshire, Augustinian abbey of St Peter and St Paul</orgName> <p>This
                     attribution was rejected in the second edition of Medieval Libraries of Great
                     Britain (1964), which did not change in the Supplement (1987). The
                     corresponding Medieval Libraries of Great Britain index card records the
                     following information, which was deemed unsatisfactory for an attribution (this
                     evidence relates instead to Peterbourgh):</p> <p>On last page: <q>iii idus
                     marcii obiit dompnus <persName>Robertus wermyngton</persName> sacerdos viiiº
                     id. mayi ob. <persName>Joh. Rychemund</persName> iiijº id. jan. ob.
                     <persName>Robertus keteryng</persName> monachi et professi monasterii
                     apostolorum Petri et [etc].</q> M. R. James suggests Bourne. Cf. Lambeth Palace
                     Library MSS 9, 327.</p></provenance>
